+## Recent view — thirteen breadcrumbs
+
+<a id="recent-01"></a>
+### 1. Who actually corrected the FAA's inaccurate answer?
+
+**Clue:** DOT OIG found that three executives learned the Commission answer misstated when the Air Force liaison joined the FAA bridge and did not act to correct it. OIG did not establish intentional deception. The recommendation to correct the answer is held; the actual later correction and receipt remain unlocated in our collection. [OIG CC-2006-085, printed pp. 9–10](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf).
+
+**Follow:** The corrected answer and attachments, version history, transmittal and Commission acknowledgment; the signed action or no-action determination, reasons, notification and case-specific follow-up/implementation entry. Keep the original submission separate from a later correction. Three executives and two current executives recommended for consideration of action are different descriptions, not an established numerical contradiction.
+
+**Test:** A timely delivered correction and documented reasoned disposition would weaken an ongoing noncorrection account. Evidence of deliberate prevention or knowingly false closure would strengthen an accountability concern. A recommendation or aggregate closure statistic settles neither. Existing leads **1–3**, FAA **PD01–PD03**.
+
+<a id="recent-02"></a>
+### 2. Which follow-up policy actually governed that case?
+
+**Clue:** The captured FAA catalog entry dates Order 2900.1, *Audit Followup*, as cancelled September 30, 2006, but offers no text. A separate November 2006 financial-audit memorandum cites DOT 8000.1C. These observations do not establish the rule governing this investigation. [Catalog study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/039ab61ff0bae307f052bb9a3aa7a05a4b6e79f2/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-audit-followup-catalog-2026-10-29/README.md); [same-year citation study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/db86a3fb3530d4c8e207f6f3a9c11bd5f3a8b1cf/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-2006-policy-citation-2026-10-29/README.md).
+
+**Follow:** The actual order and amendments; cancellation approval, effective provisions and successor; office-transfer/implementation records; and the case's actual routing and follow-up record. Preserve AFM-100 as the cancellation-note value and ABU-100 as the catalog's office-of-primary-responsibility value.
+
+**Test:** A routine supersession with continuous applicable follow-up would weaken a policy-gap theory. A documented case-relevant change or exception requires examination on its actual terms. Temporal proximity alone does not establish purpose, a missed deadline or a gap. Existing lead **3**, **PD04**.
