+
+<a id="recent-10"></a>
+### 10. Where is the November airline interview the catalog describes?
+
+**Clue:** NARA's index/catalog 2609600 describes a November 19, 2003 nine-page interview, but its exposed PDF displays an April 26, 2004 three-page SOC memorandum. Catalog 2609603 supplies another form of the April memorandum. [Interview-source review and exact source pins](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0fef3ac823ba30a09f16fcac8b6452f9fe1bca50/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-source-interview-controls-2026-10-29/README.md).
+
+**Follow:** The actual November interview, original interview audio/notes and archival accession/file-association/version records. Keep catalog description, exposed link, downloaded body and physical page count separate.
+
+**Test:** An indexing/export association error is a live alternative to substitution or removal. The two April forms differ in bytes, page dimensions and extracted/image representations; tracked statements appear in both, without an exhaustive equivalence finding. Recovering the November original would permit the intended comparison. Existing leads **7, 28, 30**, **TEL02/TEL04**, **TI01/TI02/TI07**.
+
+<a id="recent-11"></a>
+### 11. Were the disputed airline–FAA accounts describing the same call?
+
+**Clue:** Interview accounts differ on when American learned United was missing an aircraft relative to a Herndon contact. Staff-report note 259 concerns missing-United notification/ground-stop decisions; a separate paragraph/note 264 describes a 9:16 call. Arpey's 8:05–8:10 passage is explicitly under a Central Time convention and does not expressly identify the same call. [Source comparison and premise qualification](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0fef3ac823ba30a09f16fcac8b6452f9fe1bca50/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-source-interview-controls-2026-10-29/README.md).
