+**Follow:** Contemporaneous SOC/call logs; the FAA ATCSCC NOM Line 5149, position 34B source and AAL transcript; AAL's separately cited April 26 and July 7, 2004 answers; SOC chronology and staff citation papers. Match participants, call legs, subjects, events and clock conventions before comparing times.
+
+**Test:** Multiple calls, different personnel knowledge and acknowledged recall limits could reconcile the accounts. An authenticated same-call inconsistency would be more probative than differences between loosely joined memories. A conditional time-zone conversion does not calibrate historical clocks. Existing leads **7, 30**, **TEL02/TEL04**, **TI03/TI04**.
+
+<a id="recent-12"></a>
+### 12. Was an aircraft-warning request delivered, and what information controls were imposed?
+
+**Clue:** SOC personnel reported no received Herndon request to warn cockpits and no management warning decision. The memorandum also attributes an information-containment instruction and restricted internal Flight 11 manifest access. These are distinct participant accounts, not a demonstrated suppression mechanism. [SOC pp. 2–3 and preserved observations](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0fef3ac823ba30a09f16fcac8b6452f9fe1bca50/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-source-interview-controls-2026-10-29/README.md).
+
+**Follow:** Actual request/receipt and dispatch records, warning messages, decision logs, instruction/policy versions, distribution lists and manifest-access records. Determine scope, timing, recipients and operational effects separately.
+
+**Test:** Confusion, a failed handoff or ordinary operational information controls could explain the accounts. Evidence of timely notification and legitimate control purposes must be retained; a documented decision to withhold a known actionable warning would justify a stronger inquiry. Existing leads **7, 30**, **TEL02/TEL04**, **TI05**. This is not the separate Moussaoui-to-FAA warning in lead 47.
+
+<a id="recent-13"></a>
+### 13. Did reported post-impact tracks represent real aircraft positions?
+
+**Clue:** The SOC memorandum records statements about tracks associated with AA11 continuing south and AA77 continuing west after their respective impacts. These are reported display observations, not acquired raw radar or independent aircraft-position measurements. [ASD/TSD source distinctions](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0fef3ac823ba30a09f16fcac8b6452f9fe1bca50/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-source-interview-controls-2026-10-29/README.md).
+
+**Follow:** Actual ASD/TSD feeds and track identifiers, source attribution, coasting/extrapolation and update/latency definitions, playback settings and independently calibrated clocks. Technical evaluation remains with the assigned technical investigation; none is newly performed in this list.
+
+**Test:** Stale/extrapolated displays, track association or timing could explain apparent continuation. Only authenticated contemporaneous measurements with known semantics could discriminate those possibilities from a real inconsistent trajectory. Existing leads **7, 32**, **TI06** and the technical clock/radar register.
