+# Earlier research leads and qualifications
+
+These eleven contexts were recovered or clarified from earlier work. They are not eleven new independently verified events. Source eligibility and contrary explanations remain part of each item.
+
+<a id="early-01"></a>
+### EARLY-01 — Premature CNN/BBC collapse reporting and the missing upstream message
+
+The September 2 package preserved distinct CNN hedging/qualification and more definite BBC reports of completed collapse before the building fell. The unresolved lead is the original message, sender, wording and basis, rather than a presumed demolition timetable.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** Archive item titles plus offsets are not certified broadcaster clocks. Expected-collapse warnings, rumor or identification error remain ordinary alternatives. This revision does not re-listen to the broadcasts or authenticate network masters.
+
+**Open TODO:** Original Reuters/wire bulletin and correction; newsroom rundowns/source calls; broadcaster timecode and complete uncut source chain.
+
+**Citations:** [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-55ace1170d733541); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-e215cfd7f0c3df45); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-2e8ae0928f3985bc). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-02"></a>
+### EARLY-02 — Hayden, Catalano and the distinction between morning escape and afternoon warnings
+
+The held warning-chain audit acquired the Catalano MFR and preserved Hayden/CNN accounts. It distinguishes morning evacuation and tower-collapse-related escape recollections from afternoon deformation concern and withdrawal.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** The MFR is already held and must not be listed as missing. Its retrospective opinions are not instrument readings or an afternoon forecast; related accounts and an agent review are not independent event measurements.
+
+**Open TODO:** Associated notes/recordings, NIST engineering follow-up, transit measurements/operator records, actual command-to-newsroom transmissions and independent clocks.
+
+**Citations:** [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-e215cfd7f0c3df45); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-2e8ae0928f3985bc). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-03"></a>
+### EARLY-03 — AFA off-site alarm test history, ordinary baseline and unlocated originals
+
+The later source audit inspected NIST's account of the roughly 06:47 test entry, recorded 10:00:52 fire condition, expiry and later operator-clear entries, and the account of preceding daily tests.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** Off-site test behavior is not disabling every building detector. Later suggested system/link failure is an inference, not a timestamped failure measurement. A recorded surname cannot identify a person reliably; the daily pattern proves neither proper maintenance nor illicit preparation.
+
+**Open TODO:** Original July 16, 2003 AFA letter, complete history, service/authorization requests, code/clock definitions and a longer testing baseline; completed failed routes remain completed.
+
+**Citations:** [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-4d1ed205e721ba3d). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-04"></a>
+### EARLY-04 — DTA 817373 contractor/equipment records and the missing Exhibit 14 originals
+
+The held April 3, 2003 Tribunal decision supplies CCTV maintenance and equipment-procurement evidence and original-exhibit locators, including invoice 12318 and separate maintenance records.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** The earlier pasted account's October 2001 determination is a separate source stage. December 1, 1994 dates a different maintenance invoice, not automatically invoice 12318. Ordinary-maintenance evidence is positive counterevidence to unexplained-procurement claims; 2001 access or sabotage is not established.
+
+**Open TODO:** Original Exhibit 14, 1990 proposal, contract, equipment inventory, actual invoice/payment originals and dated 2001 access/work records. Exact-source searches did not recover the original packet.
+
+**Citations:** [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-db2d9632ecb9eb3e); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-5766f205777bf35f); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-b5a7853d425511cc). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-05"></a>
+### EARLY-05 — Directed thermite cutting: engineering feasibility is not a WTC 7 installation finding
+
+An early engineering discussion cited a government-hosted directed-thermite study and separated contained cutting devices from loose thermite. It supplies a device-specific feasibility question that a generic loud-blast exclusion does not settle.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** The old assistant statement and cited study are not evidence of installation, quantity, placement, timing or successful cutting of WTC 7 members. Roof-point motion cannot by itself establish removal of every supporting column or the agent that removed support.
+
+**Open TODO:** Exact study version and tested dimensions; authenticated same-geometry capacity, placement/quantity/heat-transfer/timing and residue/custody evidence, with matched fire alternatives.
+
+**Citations:** [dated message excerpts and original byte/line locators](CITATIONS.md#reference-a5f75e2ba0f1fcdd); [Earlier supplied source 1](https://www.osti.gov/bridge/servlets/purl/1344-QDsu9M/webviewable/1344.pdf). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-06"></a>
+### EARLY-06 — HBI briquette operation versus other explosive operations at the same project
+
+Participant-origin sources distinguish a mechanically initiated upper briquette-section collapse from explosive reactor demolition and a gas-plant cut-and-pull operation. The later source-association report retains a specific recording candidate.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** The entire project was not nonexplosive. Source association is not an authenticated ID-to-method attestation. The planned motion comparison failed to acquire eligible video, so no new visual, acoustic or acceleration result exists.
+
+**Open TODO:** Actual eligible recording/custody and dated operation-to-video crosswalk; only then perform a declared comparison with geometry/loading/edit/clock limits.
+
+**Citations:** [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-384e67d567ed2a7d); [held source audit](CITATIONS.md#reference-9b353d3e40c19840). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-07"></a>
+### EARLY-07 — Jennings/Hess and Bartmer interview accounts require event-specific clocks and source attribution
+
+The supplied research summary preserves explosion-like/destructive-event recollections and links later interview/transcript forms. It distinguishes what witnesses perceived from identification of a physical source.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** These are recalled perceptions and derivative/interview editions, not laboratory blast identification. Synchronization with the tower collapses and WTC 7 events remains necessary; no homicide or common-sponsor inference follows.
+
+**Open TODO:** Earliest complete interview recordings and dates, unedited lead-ins, speaker/location/clock joins and competing acoustic/structural explanations.
+
+**Citations:** [supplied historical attachment](CITATIONS.md#reference-05c985127d223222); [supplied historical attachment](CITATIONS.md#reference-f140ed4082b81fe3); [Earlier supplied source 1](https://subsaga.com/bbc/documentaries/crime/the-conspiracy-files/series-2/2-9-11-the-truth-behind-the-third-tower.html); [Earlier supplied source 2](https://www.indybay.org/newsitems/2009/04/20/18590521.php); [Earlier supplied source 3](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-IfgYhjQ9fE). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-08"></a>
+### EARLY-08 — Other chemical-marker claims retain ordinary-material alternatives
+
+The supplied summary records a 1,3-diphenylpropane argument alongside NIST's reported plastics/polystyrene explanation and general USGS dust findings.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** These cited discussions are not a same-sample assay or WTC 7-specific thermite test. A chemical's presence or plausibility is not unique identification of a demolition material; this revision performs no chemistry replication.
+
+**Open TODO:** Original measurements, sample/building/source and custody joins, reference-material controls, phase/formation conditions and a discriminating same-region analysis.
+
+**Citations:** [supplied historical attachment](CITATIONS.md#reference-05c985127d223222); [Earlier supplied source 1](https://www.nist.gov/world-trade-center-investigation/study-faqs/wtc-7-investigation); [Earlier supplied source 2](https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/ofr01429); [Earlier supplied source 3](https://scholars.duke.edu/publication/682899). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-09"></a>
+### EARLY-09 — Tower descent timing must distinguish a roof feature, destruction front, dust and debris
+
+The earlier discussion explicitly distinguished roughly 9–11-second first-exterior-debris timing from the complete descent of an entire building. This is a methodological correction to a common collapse-time inference.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** It is not an independently calibrated tower trajectory or validation of every NIST detail. WTC 7's measured north-roofline interval concerns a different building, tracked feature and event.
+
+**Open TODO:** Original multi-camera geometry/cadence, identifiable material points, event definitions and uncertainty before acceleration/force or mechanism comparisons.
+
+**Citations:** [dated message excerpts and original byte/line locators](CITATIONS.md#reference-a5f75e2ba0f1fcdd); [Earlier supplied source 1](https://www.nist.gov/world-trade-center-investigation/study-faqs/wtc-towers-investigation). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-10"></a>
+### EARLY-10 — Later Floor 7 human-review export remains unaccepted evidence input
+
+The supplied guided-review JSON has sixteen rows and a summary of twelve recorded entries. It explicitly records human_accepted=false, local review not submitted/accepted, and null actual_D/model_discrepancies.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** test_only=false does not make the review scientifically accepted. An empty missing list is not proof that every row or downstream engineering quantity is confirmed. Earlier northeast stills, this later packet and graph-axis coordinates are separate inputs.
+
+**Open TODO:** Complete applicable source/row/time and acceptance checks; preserve literal observations, outlines and uncertainty before any discrepancy or glass-state/physics calculation.
+
+**Citations:** [supplied historical attachment](CITATIONS.md#reference-f0c0780b56e65783). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
+
+<a id="early-11"></a>
+### EARLY-11 — The supplied March 2002 Forward article is a distinct, qualified news source
+
+Text extraction confirms the supplied article's title, Marc Perelman byline and March 15, 2002 date. Its intelligence-operation reporting is attributed to sources, while the same article includes a no-prior-knowledge account.
+
+**Context / contrary evidence:** This is press reporting, not a laboratory disposition or original operational-tasking record. It must not be conflated with a differently titled later Forward article, treated as confirmed chemical evidence, or counted as an independent FBI investigation.
+
+**Open TODO:** Underlying on-record/source documents, actual government tasking/receipt and person/company joins, and original final chemistry/custody records. Existing UMS tests remain open.
+
+**Citations:** [article identity and text-review record](CITATIONS.md#reference-dd2e2fb9379f14a8). External targets are inherited citation/retrieval leads unless the linked audit records actual source inspection.
