+# WTC 7 prioritized verification steps and decisive tests
+
+October 25, 2026. A planning view of the [131-entry master register](CITATIONS.md#reference-c12ac1734416eb71), organized into 20 overlapping work groups. This is a proposed order of investigation value and dependencies, not a probability ranking of causes. Every M ID is mapped below; a mapped correction or completed finding is not automatically an outstanding experiment.
+
+The highest-value work connects independently justified inputs to independently scored observations. Start with source/run identity, effective heating, and usable motion constraints; then test the initiating connection, transfer, propagation, and observed descent. In parallel, pursue authenticated audio and physical-evidence links that could discriminate intervention from other explanations. Lower-ranked documentary leads stay open where evidence justifies them; prioritization is not a closed topic list.
+
+This dated plan distinguishes held-source audits from the native scientific tests that remain open. It does not establish a causal ranking.
