+## Source version and meaning of completion
+
+The input is the October 25 master register, SHA-256 `a07207beb20d6f6642108282ec43c91bf4a6e6d68895d6bffb12744ed00a63d4`, preserved in the [planning review record](CITATIONS.md#local-ee3e0fd46f7602de). The master controls entry wording, source links and qualifications; this note controls only this proposed work order. A later material update to that register requires a priority/status review. That review has now been made for V01; the updated master SHA-256 is `9caf4cd2b61305dcc8f9682bdf54c763c84dac7492ccd27a592f711cb22d5ea6`. The original planning-input snapshot remains preserved, and the V01 revision record preserves the immediate preceding master and plan. The later V02 source/provenance audit is now reflected below; at V02 integration its master SHA-256 was `8ea9a1840fed671bb75049f10b4c0c5476f2e7ba67b2586c715871327c0ce0e1`. The [V02 review record](CITATIONS.md#local-f7d8bcbae5200fa3) preserves the immediately preceding V01 master/plan and the new diff. The October26 V03 integration had master SHA-256 `3575ec76865e27510ef84625dc928ac2c17f146e8371ebd1638a0a0955755233`; its [review record](CITATIONS.md#local-118a63f873a78460) preserves the immediate V02 master/plan and new diff. At V04 integration the master SHA-256 was `e55307e7cedc4b2081e75aad362e68951c5b0395a5b0663016b0721fcdd81df1`; its [review record](CITATIONS.md#local-2cc3e4eb34b3b06e) preserves the immediate V03 context and current diff. At V05 integration the master SHA-256 was `894523523d787a56d8e089beaa5501204fb5f3f5309fd4d8ab273f0fad3b74a8`; its [review record](CITATIONS.md#local-de2b07b26bad81ac) preserves the immediate V04 context and new diff. The October 28 reassessment now has current master SHA-256 `ec1d1495853ff1749368b78c19e2c263a574c08f1aeb72522646533104a7d804`; its [review record](CITATIONS.md#local-2ed08e5fd60307d6) preserves the immediately preceding context and text diff.
+
+**VERIFY** means check a claim, version, source or effective setting. **RETRIEVE** means identify or obtain a specific missing dependency through an authorized route. **MEASURE** means establish an observation and its uncertainty. **TEST** means compare specified alternatives under justified conditions. **KEEP** means retain an established finding, negative result or qualification without repeating completed work merely to produce another result. The original list was a plan. The user-authorized V01 source pass, V02 held-record baseline-authentication audit and V03 source/constraint pass and V04 thermal source/semantics audit and V05 candidate/source/runtime audit have now been performed to their recorded scopes. V02 did not authenticate a complete historical executed baseline. V03 rechecks source/frame/configuration and saved diagnostic arithmetic without a new accepted calibrated trajectory or physical-consequence test. V05 did not reproduce the native baseline or diagnose the two recorded stiffness warnings. No model, waveform or laboratory test was run. Other proposed actions retain their unperformed status unless separately documented.
+
+Keep four completion levels distinct: source clarification; numerical reproduction; physical validation within tested conditions; historical inference. A successful replay does not validate installed geometry or actual heating. A model mismatch challenges the specified prediction, not every fire mechanism. Prescribed support removal does not identify its historical means. Missing records and failed access are not evidence of intent.
+
+Before any decisive comparison, state the exact proposition, source/input versions, observable, justified parameter domain, uncertainty, held-out evidence, acceptance rule, and bounded protocol/repair limits. Preserve unchanged controls, null results, failed variants and contrary findings. Tolerances must come from numerical and observation uncertainty, not be chosen to make a preferred explanation pass. A result can decisively resolve a narrow proposition while leaving the historical cause unresolved.
