+
+**Would strengthen a validation claim:** independent applicable data predict the relevant response with justified uncertainty. **Would weaken it:** the comparison reuses fit data, omits the needed failure mode, or changes material/conditions without a validated bridge. TN2269's non-failing connection comparison does not validate hot fracture; genuine experimental agreement still counts within its domain. Matching a component or another solver does not validate the entire WTC 7 sequence, and historical rarity is not a numerical cause probability. A conservative choice must name the response and direction; some assumptions enhance resistance.
+
+**Dependency:** original data and exact comparison identities; this audit informs V08–V15 rather than creating a universal pass/fail. Sources: [original connection experiments](CITATIONS.md#local-48b09de49f648db1), [furnace-sag trace](CITATIONS.md#local-aab0d3204843ef99), [TN2269 comparison](CITATIONS.md#local-9ae95f7dde24b399), and [causal-chain synthesis](CITATIONS.md#local-35078f47f1bd0711).
+
+## Retain completed findings and record the actual outcome
+
+Do not redo the completed source-hash integration, material-definition search, constant-25 duplication count, original digital audio-bin calculation, failed CBS continuity shortcut, or passive UAF parsing merely to count new work. Their remaining questions concern interpretation, source/run identity, applicability and consequence. Preserve the fifteen correction bullets in the master, especially affirmative physical evidence, real residual contact/support, existing sensitivity studies, and results that weaken blanket criticisms. A newly available source or a demonstrated defect can justify a specifically bounded recheck.
+
+For each future unit, record what was actually verified, retrieved, measured or tested; exact inputs and versions; observable results and uncertainty; unchanged controls and contrary outcomes; what narrow proposition changed; and what remains unresolved. Distinguish a failed access route or missing runtime from a negative physical finding. Do not silently widen the scope, repair the baseline, infer intent, or mark a historical explanation proved from a successful numerical fit.
+
+The [initial coverage map](CITATIONS.md#local-52b2d96cb5bef607) preserves the original primary work-group assignments and retained-finding roles. The [current V04 progress map](CITATIONS.md#local-f80b2495a61d2fa1) retains V01/V02/V03 checks and adds thermal-source/processing distinctions without claiming authenticated historical effective values; the archived initial planned-status labels are not current completion claims. The initial planning review remains preserved. The V01 [revision checklist](CITATIONS.md#local-0a6699fe25786979), [text diff](CITATIONS.md#local-fe15cc464cb39be4) and [verification results](CITATIONS.md#local-bd67c1c6f229bd6d) document the current source-check update. The V01 update performs held-record attribution review only; no listed model, waveform or physical-consequence test was performed.
