+# Investigation catalogue — public research edition
+
+October 30, 2026. This edition publishes the maintained catalogue through received update 050, including all fifteen later source findings and the steel minute-approval qualification. It is a research publication derived from a broader private working catalogue; it does not establish a collapse cause, conspiracy conclusion or completion percentage.
+
+The overlapping populations are **175 extended-master entries, 370 source findings, 49 consolidated leads, 13 recent breadcrumbs, 38 later report bodies/37 units, 247 documentary claim/text units and eleven recovered earlier contexts**. Historical research items retain their original numbering. Entries sharing a source are not independent evidence and must not be added as votes or probabilities.
+
+The fifteen finding additions are FA044, PL022–PL029 and NR068–NR073. They retain conditional event-order limits, Spanish identification/transaction qualifications, CIA accountability/disclosure and denominator issues, and source/citation corrections. The steel approval is distinct from exact approved-text identity, agreement execution, transport, receipt, cutting and specimen custody. FAA schedule and catalog associations remain distinct from executed transfers and case-specific outcomes.
+
+The telephone byte comparison retains the re-encoding alternative, all count/seek mismatches and unfinished semantic/runtime/source tests. The method qualification is now public: **“independent decoder” means previous standalone FFmpeg output**; independent decoder validation was not performed. [Published qualification](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b30daf0f664b8688b18dea4fa08587a12dbefa97/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-sound-controls-2026-10-30/method-qualification-2026-10-30/METHOD-QUALIFICATION.md).
+
+The subsequent same-decoder comparison reports fitted-overlap correlations near 0.958 and 0.916, while retaining an unexamined Ong suffix of nominally 6.475 seconds in the derived view. Related signal structure qualifies what byte differences alone imply; it does not establish identical words, full coverage, actual playback, speakers or historical clocks. [Report and all unmatched-region limits](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6dffea2a1a83972f3fad87c2e6ba4d39473099f8/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-signal-alignment-2026-10-30/README.md).
+
+## Reader and source routes
+
+- [Master leads](MASTER-LEADS.md) and [370 source findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md).
+- [Consolidated leads and recent breadcrumbs](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md).
+- [Later source reports and qualifications](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md).
+- [All 247 earlier documentary claim units](DOCUMENTARY-CLAIMS.md), with earlier verdicts retained as claims to test.
+- [Eleven earlier research contexts](EARLIER-CHAT-AUDIT.md).
+- [Historical research items](HISTORICAL-CONTEXT.md) and the dated [priority plan](PRIORITY-PLAN.md).
+- [Citation routes and unavailable originals](CITATIONS.md), [publication scope and review](PUBLICATION-REVIEW.md), and [payload manifest](PUBLICATION.json).
+
+Original studies control their own methods and acceptance. Supplied URLs are citation leads unless an owning report records inspection. Normalized public data preserve research content while excluding private file locators and administration. Unpublished originals remain explicit gaps; a pointer is not new authentication. This edition excludes lawsuit strategy, private correspondence, mailbox/attachment inventories, chat transcripts, credentials and local identifying paths. The private source catalogue remains separately preserved.
+
+Run `python3 investigation/catalogue/tools/verify.py` from this repository. Structural/source-snapshot verification does not independently validate historical events or scientific conclusions. Later source deliveries after update 050 require their own explicit reconciliation.
+
+## Readable research guide
+
+## Observed building motion and model validation
+
+- **Predicted upper-wall deformation is absent from the footage.** NIST acknowledges a late-stage model/observation mismatch and omitted contributions from cladding, partitions and interior walls. Its implications for initiation and later propagation must be tested separately. [M001–M003](MASTER-LEADS.md#m001).
+- **Penthouse and roofline timing do not uniformly agree.** Published comparisons use different event definitions and alignment conventions; the reported screenwall/west-penthouse ordering can reverse. A simple clock shift cannot fix a genuine same-event reversal, but matched views and events remain necessary. [M004–M008](MASTER-LEADS.md#m004), [M068](MASTER-LEADS.md#m068).
+- **The approximately 2.25-second free-fall interval requires a force-accounted sequence.** Lower-floor support failure can in principle permit upper stories to approach gravitational acceleration. The unresolved question is whether the specified historical sequence reproduces the observed interval, coherence and residual forces; a roof point is not automatically a fixed body's center of mass. [M009](MASTER-LEADS.md#m009), [M067](MASTER-LEADS.md#m067).
+- **Some printed timing comparisons contain internal offsets or event ambiguities.** Panel/caption clocks, displacement endpoints and a measured/predicted 12.9-second comparison need run/event provenance. An inferred interior-event proxy is not an independently observed initiating event. [M085](MASTER-LEADS.md#m085), [M093–M096](MASTER-LEADS.md#m093), [M129](MASTER-LEADS.md#m129).
+- **Current motion measurements remain conditional.** Saved-project versus printed series alter fitted costs; image-localization diagnostics do not yet supply calibrated material-point trajectories. Original camera clocks, geometry, edit/cadence history and unused validation observations remain important. [M118–M119](MASTER-LEADS.md#m118).
+- **“Within its own footprint” has not been established by this investigation.** FEMA maps/photos and the received human observations supply testable geometry and provenance questions; they do not substitute for a measured footprint or a full failure-sequence comparison. [Consolidated lead 36](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-36).
+
+## Fires, thermal assignments and initialized state
+
+- **Some floor fire histories were shifted from another floor.** Floor 11/13 histories derived from Floor 12, acknowledged potential overestimation and image-time assumptions warrant sensitivity tests. Sparse observations do not by themselves prove the substitutions invalid. [M010–M013](MASTER-LEADS.md#m010), [M069](MASTER-LEADS.md#m069).
+- **Unequal repeated thermal-node assignments are real file observations.** The later held-record audit reproduces 170,491 unequal-TS node IDs. Their repetition is not itself a demonstrated applied temperature or a count of independent physical errors; the historical solver's processing and echoed state remain unresolved. [M014–M017](MASTER-LEADS.md#m014).
+- **ANSYS commands also contain unequal repeated values at selected nodes.** The node 32223 example and source call order are verified, but the extreme was selected after scanning. Neither last-row interpretation nor a final temperature of 25 is established without the operative settings and output. [M089–M092](MASTER-LEADS.md#m089).
+- **Generic FSI code exists, while the historical workflow remains unauthenticated.** A completed candidate-body screen does not identify the exact WTC 7 generator, transforms, repeated-load handling or executed effective temperatures. Temperature transfer and structural-damage transfer are separate branches. [M017–M020](MASTER-LEADS.md#m017).
+- **Accumulated fire damage is initialized into a short dynamic calculation.** The 3.5/4.0-hour transition, instantaneous damage application, coarse damage mapping and residual-state continuity require matched state/output records. Earlier stable controls with shorter horizons do not by themselves settle long-term stability. [M021–M030](MASTER-LEADS.md#m021), [M096](MASTER-LEADS.md#m096).
+- **A supplied termination precedes the temperature-ramp endpoint.** This is an exact input/time relationship, not a finding that the historical run reached a particular temperature or stopped for the asserted physical reason. [M128](MASTER-LEADS.md#m128).
+- **Fireproofing, fuel and equipment applicability remain specific input questions.** Property-data qualifications, older benchmark datasets and actual installed/shutdown/cooling conditions need case-linked records. Hypothetical fuel scenarios and visible flames do not establish burned quantity or steel temperature. [M062–M064](MASTER-LEADS.md#m062), [M124](MASTER-LEADS.md#m124), [Consolidated lead 35](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-35).
+
+## Connections, restraint and propagation
+
+- **Connection calibration is not independent experimental validation.** Matching energy does not ensure the force history matches throughout failure; grouping and temperature-transfer criteria add assumptions. Later experiments reveal useful differences but do not automatically validate or invalidate the historical implementation. [M032–M037](MASTER-LEADS.md#m032).
+- **Column 79 restraint is more complicated than “unsupported.”** Support annotations, contact and surviving load paths matter. Explicit contact selections contradict a blanket inference of no coupling or residual support. [M038–M039](MASTER-LEADS.md#m038), [M122](MASTER-LEADS.md#m122).
+- **A2001 geometry and support-loss criteria remain disputed.** Corrected seat dimensions, the stiffener/side-plate question and residual stiffened-flange capacity require the same floor, installed detail, loads, temperature and contact formulation. Preliminary text includes side-cover/contact considerations; total-omission claims are too broad. [M042–M044](MASTER-LEADS.md#m042), [M072–M074](MASTER-LEADS.md#m072).
+- **Floor modifications and precursor idealizations may change restraint.** Floor 10 additions, boundary/heating assumptions, selected failure regions, studs/deck welds, slab treatment, post-buckling criteria, live load and camber deserve matched comparisons. The net direction of their combined effect is not established. [M075–M081](MASTER-LEADS.md#m075).
+- **Column 44 has a precise event-sequence question.** Bolt and buckling times must be reconciled with the narrative using actual component states and run identity. Those are accelerated-calculation times, not independently measured historical failure times. [M045](MASTER-LEADS.md#m045).
+- **Cross-core and exterior propagation require quantitative load paths.** The floor cascade, truss counterfactual, exterior unloading/sway and Floor 5/substation boundaries cannot be validated by a verbal domino sequence. Lower support and impact idealizations must not be conflated. [M030–M031](MASTER-LEADS.md#m030), [M083–M084](MASTER-LEADS.md#m083).
+- **Material-law and fracture questions have both positive and contrary controls.** Later fracture research motivates testing; an apparent published A36/A572 duplication was not reproduced in the examined released definitions. A populated field/old-manual mismatch does not select the historical solver interpretation. [M082](MASTER-LEADS.md#m082), [M120–M121](MASTER-LEADS.md#m120).
+- **“Conservative” is response-specific.** Some assumptions enhance capacity while others remove mechanisms. Matching free thermal expansion does not guarantee matching restrained forces; a synthetic counterexample demonstrates that inference limit, not an identified error in NIST's historical run. [M061](MASTER-LEADS.md#m061), [M087–M088](MASTER-LEADS.md#m087).
+
+## Released files, provenance and review
+
+- **Initially omitted LS-DYNA files were later supplied.** Keep the acknowledged correction alongside the original omission. The null-filled thermal file, geometry-version differences and six referenced load names remain distinct questions; arithmetic alone does not identify a missing physical record. [M046–M049](MASTER-LEADS.md#m046).
+- **Historical counts and filenames remain partly unreconciled.** Case B and overall totals, the commented 4.1-hour reference and same-name/different-content files require content and version joins. A comment is not an active run instruction. [M050–M054](MASTER-LEADS.md#m050).
+- **The exact executed modeling package is not reconstructed.** Positive archive/member and assembly checks narrow the gaps, but specific build, curve/material, restart, state/output and figure-generation joins remain. A modern runnable candidate would not by itself authenticate the historical run. [M029](MASTER-LEADS.md#m029), [M040–M041](MASTER-LEADS.md#m040), [M054](MASTER-LEADS.md#m054).
+- **The original five-category request is broader than a filename list.** Forty technical entries were tentatively mapped against its wording. This is not forty proven omissions or a complete semantic review of production and withholding. [Consolidated lead 33](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-33).
+- **A ten-question technical request and NIST reply are now held.** The response links questions to FAQs/errata; actual STENG-2119/R1 manuscripts and complete journal-review records remain unlocated. Nonacquisition does not establish suppression or improper rejection. [M132–M134](MASTER-LEADS.md#m132).
+- **Media and archive metadata have their own incongruities.** AVI dimensions/codec labels, CDX versus replay layers, player versions and a release lacking the penthouse segment require entity/source distinctions. They do not independently prove altered historical footage. [M097–M100](MASTER-LEADS.md#m097).
+
+## UAF and comparator controls
+
+- **UAF has source/version and graphic-label discrepancies too.** A hidden W24x55 raster label beneath a visible W21x44 presentation and repaired-archive lineage require version checking; neither alone demonstrates a changed physical result. [M101–M102](MASTER-LEADS.md#m101).
+- **A native UAF candidate is held but not independently replayed.** Log warnings, an enabled linear-static case, inactive nonlinear/time-history settings and mass/hinge settings need exact case/output joins. Two negative-stiffness eigenvalues are not proof of collapse. [M103–M108](MASTER-LEADS.md#m103).
+- **P-delta criticism must be model-specific.** A particular exclusion cannot be generalized to all UAF models. Side-plate comparisons changing expansion and geometry together do not isolate either effect. [M127](MASTER-LEADS.md#m127), [M131](MASTER-LEADS.md#m131).
+- **Reported expansion figures differ under stated conditions.** An approximate 40-percent statement and a conditional 47.8-percent calculation deserve like-for-like comparison; this is not an authenticated historical temperature or initiating displacement. [M130](MASTER-LEADS.md#m130).
+- **Later research and other buildings test limited propositions.** TN2269's reported test did not fail connections; Hu's tests differ in rate/version. Plasco and Cather/Pound comparisons need applicability controls and cannot replace a WTC 7 historical reconstruction. [M125–M126](MASTER-LEADS.md#m125), [Consolidated lead 36](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-36).
+
+## Windows, sound and physical materials
+
+- **NIST's blast-nondetection argument depends on receiver conditions.** Reviewed propagation assumptions do not reproduce every obstructed urban recording path. That limits the exclusion's scope; it supplies no affirmative demonstration of an explosive device. [M055–M058](MASTER-LEADS.md#m055).
+- **There are positive sound targets, not just arguments from silence.** An excerpt has a reproducible digital-energy concentration near 13.65–13.80 seconds. Its source, perceptual identity, calibrated pressure and historical event correspondence remain unresolved. [M117](MASTER-LEADS.md#m117).
+- **The user's noise/screams and “another explosion” observation remains preserved.** The anchor's possible-truck qualification and the distinction between a spoken description and an actual event inventory must remain. B/C/D listening/source verification is separate from ASR or waveform work. [Consolidated lead 38](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-38).
+- **Early window stills cannot establish collapse-time glass conditions.** Human row/location/appearance judgments and adjusted outlines are retained; dark spots alone cannot identify absent glass, pressure direction or mechanism. The map 5-174 reference is to Figure 5-145, not 5-143. [Consolidated lead 37](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-37).
+- **Witness and seismic reports require source-specific attribution.** Timing, station response, location, source identity and competing signatures remain necessary; an uncalibrated signal is not an identified blast. [M086](MASTER-LEADS.md#m086).
+- **FEMA Sample 1 records real local metallurgical effects.** Its building attribution, timing and initiating mechanism are separate questions. Candidate WTC7 labels can be traced into receipt records, but they do not authenticate an initiation-critical specimen. [M059–M060](MASTER-LEADS.md#m059), [M109–M110](MASTER-LEADS.md#m109).
+- **Dust-chip evidence has substantive competing interpretations.** Harrit's aluminum/oxygen argument has a conditional quantitative implication; Millette supplies phase/coating evidence. Different specimens, regions and preparation prevent a simple same-sample contradiction. Same-region native spectra, phase and thermal records remain important. [Consolidated leads 43–44](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-43).
+
+## Steel collection, paint tests and preservation
+
+- **Collection and preservation have both positive records and vulnerabilities.** Recovery-site souvenir removal, municipal PC/account/database/tape risks and unresolved return/control accounting warrant specific follow-up. They do not establish NIST destruction or identify which candidate was lost. [M065–M066](MASTER-LEADS.md#m065), [M111](MASTER-LEADS.md#m111), [M123](MASTER-LEADS.md#m123).
+- **Inventory editions and reported completion dates differ.** October 2004, 2006 and January 2007 references need actual editions and transmittals; roof-leak and specialized-maintenance concerns coexist with basic maintenance and later authorization. Authorization is not verified remediation. [Consolidated lead 42](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-42), [steel source findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#pt012).
+- **The complete court attachment contains 531 rows and 530 exact labels.** Repeated G0086, multi-object descriptions and nonsteel entries prevent treating rows as specimens or subtracting unlike counts to prove loss. Native object/alias/coupon/custody crosswalks remain missing. [Recent breadcrumb 6](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-06).
+- **Transfers expose exact execution questions.** The G-0006 letter is unsigned in the held copy; minutes are draft/unapproved; cutting language is conditional. Executed terms, applicable orders, cutting, shipment/receipt and before/after condition records must settle what happened. [Recent breadcrumb 7](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-07).
+- **Paint-study labels and specimen lists are inconsistent.** M-14/M-4, M-10 building/column fields and eight/nine-panel populations require native label/region/photo/calibration joins. A seven-panel retrieval list is our conditional reconstruction, not a recovered authored list. [Consolidated lead 40](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-40).
+- **WJE review timing and access may have limited testing opportunities.** Actual contracts, draft versions, WJE comments on NIST and delivery/acceptance records remain important. Published adverse comparisons and later general agreement are contrary evidence to blanket suppression. [Consolidated lead 41](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-41).
+- **Photographic and numerical sources have useful but limited controls.** HABS scene counterparts, selected tag-reading failures, summary normalization/fit-selection questions and figure/export differences narrow retrieval targets without establishing specimen identity or a temperature error. [HABS controls](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-steel-habs-original-route-2026-10-28-8c871b69), [summary-data review](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-steel-exhibit-a-row-census-2026-10-29-d84a4362), [fit-selection review](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-steel-inventory-transmittals-2026-10-29-4b467619).
+
+## FAA, NORAD and the operational chronology
+
+- **Official notification accounts changed materially.** AA77 versus phantom AA11 and UA93's reported 09:16 versus later 10:07 notice are event/flight differences, not mere rounding. DOT found insufficient evidence of knowing notification falsehood while criticizing the explanation for the UA93 omission. [M164–M165](MASTER-LEADS.md#m164).
+- **Executives knew a liaison answer was inaccurate and did not correct it.** This is distinct from the notification findings and a separate website correction. The later corrected answer/receipt and signed action/no-action outcome remain unlocated in the checked collection. [M166–M167](MASTER-LEADS.md#m166), [Recent breadcrumb 1](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-01).
+- **Recording capability and missing working records remain unresolved.** The 2005 WOC account and purported handbook applicability need effective-edition and installed-equipment checks. A blank Guidelist exists; the filled September 11 instance and named reorganization memo remain different missing records. [Consolidated leads 4–5](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-04).
+- **The controller-recollection cassette was deliberately destroyed.** This was a retrospective group account, not a live ATC channel. Its actual content, redundancy and higher-level purpose cannot be inferred merely from destruction or surviving operational audio. [Consolidated lead 6](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-06), [PS findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#pw024).
+- **FAA production scope and version differences are specific.** Reported UAL93-only guidance, legal/FBI restrictions, missing accident files and typed/handwritten/radar/aircraft-description differences need actual tasking, scope, original audio and revision joins. A blanket time shift does not explain every compared field. [FA findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#cf046).
+- **Mineta and the Commission retain conflicting PEOC timing accounts.** The named aircraft, location, exchange and inferred meaning of the order must be separated. Lost tunnel-alarm data and dependent diary/source families limit reconstruction; no stand-down conclusion is established. [M168–M171](MASTER-LEADS.md#m168).
+- **NEADS release/exercise records require native joins.** Six WAV CDs versus 21 public channel offerings, transcript/transport differences, exercise plans and actual suspension/inject/movement records concern different layers. Plans do not prove diversion; an MP3/catalog fingerprint is not a native clock package. [M172–M174](MASTER-LEADS.md#m172), [Recent breadcrumb 9](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-09).
+- **Our ASR control failed.** Generated words appeared on verified digital silence and repeated across source clips; those words and timing anchors are excluded. Later tone/cadence measurements cannot replace listening, recording lineage or independent clocks. [M175](MASTER-LEADS.md#m175), [FA findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#cf046).
+
+## CIA/FBI information handling and oversight
+
+- **A reported hold instruction and unanswered follow-up are concrete leads.** The January 2000 Mihdhar draft was not formally disseminated to its FBI addressees according to the reviews. FBI detailee access complicates “no FBI employee knew”; actual release authority, purpose and recipient receipt remain unresolved. [M153](MASTER-LEADS.md#m153), [S001](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md).
+- **A cable claims FBI notification, but external receipt is unverified.** Obtain SCALEC 134684, exact distribution and FBI-side receipt/tasking. General briefings or access to some CIA text do not establish delivery of this particular visa information. [M154](MASTER-LEADS.md#m154), [Consolidated lead 10](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-10).
+- **Electronic access silence is not a complete delivery test.** A reported possible paper-copy route and later cable access do not establish reliance; neither does an absent electronic access entry establish nobody saw it. [M161–M162](MASTER-LEADS.md#m161).
+- **Draft deletion, database decommissioning and later recovery are separate events.** The reviews do not establish when this particular draft was deleted. January/February 2004 discovery accounts and formatting explanations need version, preservation, recipient and oversight-request chronology. [M155–M160](MASTER-LEADS.md#m155).
+- **Search exclusions and assurances warrant item-level comparison.** Actual requests/amendments, EOP referrals, duplication/cost reasoning, production indexes and knowledge dates could distinguish agreed scope, poor coordination, mistake and knowing nondisclosure. Source recollection or institutional position alone cannot settle it. [Consolidated lead 12](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-12), [NR findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#pl021).
+- **Canestraro supplies specific but unverified paper-copy and interference allegations.** The alleged spring-2002 handoff, pressure, IG messages and OPR interview need original evidence. Earlier witness nondisclosure, a printed year mismatch, shared lineage and the press/court-copy identity gap remain material limitations. [Consolidated leads 48–49](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-48).
+- **CIA tape destruction impaired independent scrutiny.** Actual advice, approvals, tape-review notes, requests and disposition records remain important. The archive concerns Zubaydah/al-Nashiri, not automatically KSM; no-prosecution and source-dependence limits are retained. [Consolidated lead 13](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-13), [PT findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#ps012).
+- **Some apparent statistical discrepancies weaken on inspection.** CIA's 1,018 versus “over 1,000” CIR total is compatible; 24-person and 30-person respondent groups have different descriptions and cannot be pooled. Original interview data and receipts remain absent. [NR067](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#nr066).
+
+## Warnings, Moussaoui and the planning narrative
+
+- **The warning collection demonstrates threat awareness, not a complete receipt history.** The 71-product/101-page census includes seventy preattack items and one postattack item. Source quality, the “70 investigations” count, actual presidential receipt, tasking and implementation need their own records. [Consolidated lead 16](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-16), [PW findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#nr067).
+- **A local Moussaoui threat assessment was replaced before FAA delivery.** OIG reports headquarters withheld the seven-page local memorandum in favor of an eleven-page teletype; local agents also briefed FAA. Compare actual omitted content, oral briefing and onward routing instead of assuming either total suppression or equivalent warning. [Consolidated lead 47](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-47).
+- **Moussaoui drafts and messages preserve specific disagreements.** Exhibits 334/347/349/350/351/692/693/810 and later controls concern different purposes, dates, drafts and attachments. Six drafting objections and visible clause differences need original version/recipient joins; a court copy is not an authenticated full email thread. [Draft/advice comparison](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-moussaoui-evidence-edits-2026-10-29-c7efb3f3), [six-objection review](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-moussaoui-emergency-fisa-2026-10-28-0c0f0f91).
+- **Exhibits 636/637 identify a possible intelligence link and an anticipated handoff.** They do not supply the French/CIA material or prove receipt. Actual EC/Paris attachments, counsel advice, final package and referral/nonreferral records are the discriminators. [Recent breadcrumbs 4–5](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-04).
+- **Cole/attribution-control documents contain proposals and version gaps.** Withdrawn pages, draft/final and forwarding questions require originals. A proposal to delay public attribution pending presidential decisions could reflect operational security or an inquiry; implementation and knowingly false attribution are not established. [Consolidated leads 14–15](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-14).
+- **Parts of the planning narrative depend on controlled interrogation reporting.** Commission questioning/access limits, coercion, translation, later sources and judicial-access concerns warrant source-by-source corroboration. They do not make every statement false or establish an alternative organizer. [Consolidated lead 21](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-21), [PL findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#fa043).
+- **Seized-message and ticket dates contain unresolved stage/version differences.** Reservation, charge, purchase, issuance and later stipulation are not one event. August 24/25/27 differences and time-zone hypotheses need actual transaction history and source custody, not a merged narrative. [Consolidated lead 22](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-22), [PL018–PL021](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#pl017).
+
+## Telephone calls, recorders and radar
+
+- **Telephone release completeness and exhibit origins remain open.** Request 14's actual assembly/manifest, September 20 analysis, attachments and source-to-exhibit worksheets matter. Mirrored forms and presentation resources are held; page gaps and format differences do not prove fabrication. [Consolidated lead 28](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-28), [Recent breadcrumb 8](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-08).
+- **UA93 has both discrepancies and strong agreement controls.** All 35 candidate-paired Duration Connect readings agree; 33 full-key joins are accepted and two tentative. A separate SCP 7565/7555 and masked operator-field question remain, with units and native semantics unresolved. [Consolidated lead 29](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-29).
+- **UA175 summaries use conflicting call units/fields.** Three attempts, two reported connections and one substantiated conversation are distinct propositions. Published 75/31 values match SCP fields while selected Connect fields read 18/24; native definitions and event/recipient joins must settle meaning. [UA175 source review](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-telephone-source-interview-controls-2026-10-29-441762e5).
+- **AA77 call totals, durations and office legs remain unreconstructed.** Direct/collect, setup/connection, transfers and PBX/operator legs need carrier definitions and recipient records. A zero presentation label does not establish no conversation; a positive field does not authenticate every caller. [Consolidated lead 30](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-30).
+- **The archived recorder candidate reproduces frames but fails selected integrity checks.** The work reproduces 37,842 frames and finds two checksum-failing filled pages; three of the final 32 longitudinal codes lie on failing pages. Corruption, incomplete writing, other error and alteration remain alternatives; historical aircraft custody and installed decoding remain unverified. [Consolidated lead 31](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-31), [AVR findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#va005).
+- **Terminal values and transcript endpoints need calibrated interpretation.** Raw zero scales to about −1.083g under the tested definition, rather than necessarily zero acceleration. A last listed utterance is not automatically recorder termination; nominal transcript/impact differences are not measured clock errors. [AVR findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#va005), [VA findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#sf023), [Consolidated lead 32](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-32).
+- **The newest interview review adds a concrete catalog mismatch.** A nine-page November interview description links to a three-page April memorandum; a second April form differs digitally. Multiple calls, recall limits and time-zone conventions could reconcile some timing accounts. Actual interview/call originals remain needed. [Recent breadcrumbs 10–11](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-10).
+- **Aircraft warnings and information controls have material contrary context.** The staff report describes dispatcher warnings at 9:22 and 9:36 and a security rationale for manifest lockout. That weighs against blanket no-warning or unexplained-suppression accounts, without proving crew receipt, comprehensive coverage or proper policy application. The dated AAL letter, actual messages and logs remain missing. [Warning/QFR qualification](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-telephone-playback-controls-2026-10-29-13a63efd), [earlier breadcrumb 12](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-12).
+- **Reported post-impact display tracks require their own test.** Continuing ASD/TSD tracks need actual feeds, track identifiers, coasting/extrapolation definitions and calibrated clocks before being treated as real post-impact aircraft positions. [Recent breadcrumb 13](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#recent-13).
+
+## Saudi-linked support, informants, finance and economic interests
+
+- **Saudi-linked housing, assistance, banking and communications are substantive leads.** Particular contacts and assistance warrant original person/transaction/custody joins. The court's preliminary inferences and expert limits must remain distinct from a final finding of knowing attack support. [Consolidated leads 18–20](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-18), [M135–M152](MASTER-LEADS.md#m135).
+- **Specific bank/telephone records contain contradictions and limits.** Reimbursement assessments, a sign conflict, cash amount/source, post-bank calls, April 19/20 dates and record-window/population differences need native data. Named enclosures and line counts are not complete carrier datasets or people counts. [M143–M152](MASTER-LEADS.md#m143).
+- **The restaurant/video/drawing chain remains partly unresolved.** Witness translation/sequence limitations, a stated coincidence belief, alias and camera-operator versions, and drawing copy/custody matter. Mathematical alternatives and expert/court scope must accompany the suspicious interpretation. [M135–M142](MASTER-LEADS.md#m135).
+- **The FBI informant's $100,000 payment is documented; its purpose is not.** Authorization, voucher, delegation, conditions, full payment history and closure records must distinguish reward, relocation/legal costs or a silence theory. Noncomplicity findings, polygraph limits and interview-access restrictions remain relevant. [Consolidated lead 17](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-17), [SF findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#ct012).
+- **Abnormal options activity is a real statistical lead with contrary explanations.** Reported long-put quantiles are not probabilities of foreknowledge. Raw origin-coded trades, exposure, beneficial ownership, newsletter distribution and official supporting analyses are needed; hedging, stock losses and contemporaneous share buying must be retained. [Consolidated leads 23–24](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-23), [OP findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#st012).
+- **The ISI-directed payment claim remains rooted in anonymous reporting.** Court/FBI evidence of UAE financing and particular transfers does not authenticate that alleged instruction or every upstream sender. Nominal/net/fee/date differences and duplicate records cannot be inflated into extra transfers. [Consolidated lead 25](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-25), [IF findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#op035).
+- **Halliburton and other corporate interests present benefit/access questions, not an established operational bridge.** Procurement advantage, planning roles and oversight weaknesses deserve original approval/beneficiary/access records. Later benefit, a board relationship or a surname does not establish preattack participation. [Consolidated lead 26](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-26), [CT findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#in010).
+- **Insurance context weakens a timing-only foreknowledge argument.** Lease terrorism-coverage provisions, insurer-specific forms, occurrence disputes and rebuilding/debt obligations matter. Gross recoveries do not establish owner net profit; actual distributions and obligations remain missing inputs. [Consolidated lead 27](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-27), [IN findings](SOURCE-FINDINGS.md#if009).
+
+## Urban Moving Systems and access/security allegations
+
+- **Government association, intelligence affiliation and attack tasking are different propositions.** The FBI-reported association and particular sightings justify person/company/chronology checks; nationality or religion does not establish intelligence membership. Preattack arrival, foreknowledge and operational control remain unestablished. [Consolidated lead 45](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-45).
+- **The explosive-material trail concerns a vehicle and samples, not a confirmed substance on a person.** Canine “positive” versus “possible hit” wording, two control swabs, sample descriptions and lab routes require original handler, accession and final chemistry records. Pending language in a 2001 account is not a verified current status. [M113](MASTER-LEADS.md#m113), [UMS chemistry-source test](LATEST-SOURCE-UNITS.md#unit-telephone-ua175-summary-review-2026-10-28-3c53ee23).
+- **Photo, VHS, surveillance and White House records have precise custody gaps.** Twelve input prints/thirteen output images, a distinct enhancement lead, an uncalibrated 08:29 label and a mixed-scope finding aid require actual bodies, input/output mappings, clocks and vehicle/person matching. They are not thirteen verified emails or confirmed chemical results. [M114](MASTER-LEADS.md#m114), [Consolidated lead 46](CONSOLIDATED-AND-RECENT.md#consolidated-46).
+- **Security-contractor and former-employee accounts differ in scope and timing.** Project closeout, unfinished work, visitor-database custody and individual access/control require original records. A corporate relationship does not establish which person could perform or authorize a particular act. [M115–M116](MASTER-LEADS.md#m115).
+
+## What remains open
+
+The annotated lists retain the original missing-input and falsification tests. Completed source readings, copy comparisons, row counts, published-note checks and negative search routes remain completed; they are not counted again as unperformed scientific work. Historical run authentication, calibrated chronology, same-specimen measurements, actual recipient receipt and intent still require their respective evidence.
+
+The strongest general objection to treating this collection as cumulative proof of a single conspiracy is **dependence plus untested alternatives**: many entries concern the same source, witness, model assumption or missing join. Several suspicions weakened after exact comparison. Conversely, innocent alternatives do not erase documented noncorrection, destruction, filtering or concrete discrepancies; those need the specific tests above.
+
+Verification and limitations are recorded in REVIEW.json and COVERAGE.json. Exact text changes against the immediately preceding preserved versions accompany this update. The original master registers, source reports, raw media and earlier thirteen-item breadcrumb document remain preserved.
